## Engineering update

The course published the desk's outcome after accepting the split tickets.
The two causes ended differently: the parser was fixed, while the booking-v3 hint fix was declined
because the form was retired. Closing both tickets as completed would lose that distinction.

<ResolutionTable />

## What closure means

The parser ticket closes as **completed**, citing the desk's parser fix.
The hint ticket closes as **not planned**, citing the retirement of booking-v3.
The desk supplied these outcomes; this repository documents the investigation and does not
claim to contain the production parser fix or the form retirement implementation.

The [cause-based triage decision](/kb/decisions/0002-triage-by-cause) stays unchanged as the
accepted record. Its counts describe the export through 4 October. The engineering outcome
does not change those historical report counts or establish the root cause of every unusual body.
The unresolved bodies remain visible there; further reports need current tenant settings and
the original input and calendar evidence before being attributed to a retired path or a fixed parser.

The [incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) links to this outcome. The desk can keep using the
[cause-based triage rule](/kb/triage/dedupe) while checking new reports against current product versions.

